--------------------------------------------------------\nThe TeX Live Guide—2026 (https://tug.org/texlive/doc/texlive-en/texlive-en.html)\nciteturn10404search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; This is the program invoked for many common formats, e.g., etex, latex, pdﬂatex. ... See texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/manual/pdftex-a.pdf for the manual, and texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/samplepdftex/samplepdf.tex for example usage of some of its features.\n#### 2.3 Extensions to TeX\n\nKnuth’s original TeX itself is frozen, apart from rare bug ﬁxes. It is present in TeX Live as the program tex, and will remain so for the foreseeable future. TeX Live also contains several extended versions of TeX (also known as TeX engines), all derived from the original program.\n\ne-TeX\n    \n\nadds a set of new primitives (related to macro expansion, character scanning, classes of marks, additional debugging features, and more) and the TeX--XE T extensions for bidirectional typesetting. In default mode, e-TeX is 100% compatible with ordinary TeX. See texmf-dist/doc/etex/base/etex_man.pdf.\n\npdfTeX\n    \n\nbuilds on the e-TeX extensions, adding support for writing PDF output as well as DVI, and many non-output-related extensions. This is the program invoked for many common formats, e.g., etex, latex, pdﬂatex. Its web site is https://pdftex.org/. See texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/manual/pdftex-a.pdf for the manual, and texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/samplepdftex/samplepdf.tex for example usage of some of its features.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntexlive[57973] Master/texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/manual: pdftex manual - tex-live-commits mailing list - TeX Users Group (https://tug.tug.org/pipermail/tex-live-commits/2021-February/016695.html)\nciteturn10404search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; Crawled: last month;     Modified: trunk/Master/texmf-dist/doc/pdftex/manual/pdftex-a.pdf ... The asterisk \\type{*} before the ...     +